# Unlock probe: one swipe up and nothing else, so the swipe is the only gesture in the round and the
# freeze the user reports can be placed on a single action.
#
# The other jobs files spend their first hundred seconds on probes and gestures of their own, which
# makes "the desktop froze after unlocking" indistinguishable from "the desktop froze after the
# third lock/unlock pair". This file keeps the anchors a round is read from (two lsprobe instances,
# one periodic framewatch) and adds one rwtouch line that waits 120 s and then performs the short
# upward swipe that unlocks the device. 120 s is well after the desktop is up: in the fixguard rounds
# the first frames appear within the first two snapshots and the desktop stays up for two minutes.
#
# init waits for each line, so every background line ends with & and goes before rwtouch.
/redwood/bin/lsprobe 60 &
/redwood/bin/lsprobe 300 &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 20 --count 20 SpringBoard backboardd &
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 120 swipe 0.5 0.985 0.5 0.3 250